kspace-only crates from the start — it costs nothing and prevents an embarrassing accidental ",[33,1533,1534],{},"cargo publish"," of a crate never meant for crates.io.",[88,1537,1538,311,1540,1543,1544,1546],{},[279,1539,1483],{},[33,1541,1542],{},"cargo publish --dry-run"," catches missing metadata (license, description) and packaging issues without actually publishing — always run it before the real ",[33,1545,1534],{},", especially the first time for a new crate.",[88,1548,1549,1551,1552,1554],{},[279,1550,1492],{},": prefer ",[33,1553,92],{}," syntax over a bare optional dependency when you don't want the feature name to be implicitly tied to the dependency's crate name — it decouples your public feature-flag API from your internal dependency choices, so swapping the underlying crate later isn't a breaking change to your feature flags.",[18,1556,1558],{"id":1557},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[85,1560,1561,1578,1590,1601,1613,1622],{},[88,1562,1563,1566,1567,1570,1571,1573,1574,1577],{},[279,1564,1565],{},"Feature unification breaking builds",": if your crate's ",[33,1568,1569],{},"cfg(feature = \"x\")"," only makes sense with another crate's feature, you can't express that without ",[33,1572,132],{},"\u002F",[33,1575,1576],{},"?dep\u002Ffeat"," syntax.",[88,1579,1580,1585,1586,1589],{},[279,1581,1582,1583],{},"Optional dep without ",[33,1584,132],{}," creates an implicit feature of the same name; sometimes you want this (so users can ",[33,1587,1588],{},"features = [\"serde_json\"]","), sometimes you don't.",[88,1591,1592,1597,1598,318],{},[279,1593,1594],{},[33,1595,1596],{},"cargo build --features \"\""," is sometimes needed to override ",[33,1599,1600],{},"default-features",[88,1602,1603,1608,1609,1612],{},[279,1604,1605,1607],{},[33,1606,585],{}," and feature interaction",": read ",[33,1610,1611],{},"CARGO_FEATURE_*"," env vars in build scripts.",[88,1614,1615,1618,1619,1621],{},[279,1616,1617],{},"Profile inheritance",": a custom profile that doesn't ",[33,1620,492],{}," from another starts empty (potentially wrong optimization).",[88,1623,1624,1628,1629,723,1631,1633],{},[279,1625,1626],{},[33,1627,569],{}," can be slower at runtime than ",[33,1630,573],{},[33,1632,577],{}," despite smaller binaries.",[18,1635,1637],{"id":1636},"spot-the-bug","🧠 Spot the Bug",[14,1639,1640,1641,1643],{},"Two crates in the same dependency graph both use ",[33,1642,268],{},", with different feature needs. What actually happens at build time?",[23,1645,1646],{"language":25},[27,1647,1649],{"className":29,"code":1648,"language":25,"meta":31,"style":31},"# crate-a\u002FCargo.toml\n[dependencies]\nserde = { version = \"1\", default-features = false }\n\n# crate-b\u002FCargo.toml (also in the same build)\n[dependencies]\nserde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }\n",[33,1650,1651,1656,1660,1665,1669,1674,1678],{"__ignoreMap":31},[36,1652,1653],{"class":38,"line":39},[36,1654,1655],{},"# crate-a\u002FCargo.toml\n",[36,1657,1658],{"class":38,"line":45},[36,1659,121],{},[36,1661,1662],{"class":38,"line":51},[36,1663,1664],{},"serde = { version = \"1\", default-features = false }\n",[36,1666,1667],{"class":38,"line":57},[36,1668,181],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":180},[36,1670,1671],{"class":38,"line":63},[36,1672,1673],{},"# crate-b\u002FCargo.toml (also in the same build)\n",[36,1675,1676],{"class":38,"line":69},[36,1677,121],{},[36,1679,1680],{"class":38,"line":75},[36,1681,1682],{},"serde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }\n",[1684,1685,1686,1690,1709,1759,1766],"details",{},[1687,1688,1689],"summary",{},"Answer",[14,1691,1692,1694,1695,1697,1698,1701,1702,1705,1706,1708],{},[33,1693,268],{}," gets compiled with the ",[33,1696,272],{}," feature enabled for ",[279,1699,1700],{},"both"," crates — including ",[33,1703,1704],{},"crate-a",", which explicitly asked for ",[33,1707,291],{}," and no extra features.",[14,1710,1711,1712,1715,1716,1719,1720,1722,1723,1725,1726,1728,1729,1731,1732,1734,1735,1738,1739,1741,1742,1744,1745,1748,1749,260,1751,269,1753,1755,1756,1758],{},"Cargo's feature unification is graph-wide, not per-crate: within a single build (one ",[33,1713,1714],{},"Cargo.lock"," resolution), there is exactly ",[279,1717,1718],{},"one"," compiled version of ",[33,1721,268],{}," with ",[279,1724,1718],{}," feature set, and that set is the union of every feature requested by every crate that depends on it, anywhere in the graph. ",[33,1727,1704],{},"'s ",[33,1730,291],{}," only means \"don't turn on ",[33,1733,268],{},"'s own defaults ",[262,1736,1737],{},"from crate-a's request","\" — it does not mean \"guarantee ",[33,1740,268],{}," compiles without ",[33,1743,272],{}," no matter what else needs it.\" If ",[33,1746,1747],{},"crate-b"," (a sibling dependency, possibly many levels removed) asks for ",[33,1750,272],{},[33,1752,1704],{},[33,1754,272],{},"-enabled ",[33,1757,268],{}," too, silently, with no warning that its own more restrictive request was overridden by unification.",[14,1760,1761,1762,1765],{},"This is precisely why the \"Additive-Only Rule\" in this chapter matters: since you cannot reliably prevent a feature from being enabled by ",[262,1763,1764],{},"someone else"," in the graph, features must never change behavior in a way that would break a crate expecting them to be off — they can only ever add capability.",[14,1767,1768,1771,1772,1774],{},[279,1769,1770],{},"The lesson",": Cargo feature unification means a crate's ",[33,1773,291],{}," only affects its own request — if any other crate anywhere in the build graph requests a feature, everyone using that dependency gets it, with no per-crate opt-out.",[18,1776,1777],{"id":1687},"Summary",[14,1779,1780,1781,1379,1783,1785,1786,1788,1789,1791],{},"Features are additive conditional-compilation flags. Design them additive-only. Use ",[33,1782,132],{},[33,1784,1576],{}," for clean dep\u002Ffeature separation. Profiles control optimization and binary properties. ",[33,1787,585],{}," enables codegen and linking. CI should run fmt\u002Fclippy\u002Ftest\u002Fdoc and cross-compile. Use ",[33,1790,931],{}," for versioning and publishing. Set and test the MSRV.",[14,1793,1794],{},"Next: The deeper type system — variance, HRTBs, and tricky generics.",[1796,1797,1798],"style",{},"html .default .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-default);background: var(--shiki-default-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-default-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-default-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-default-text-decoration);}html .github-dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-github-dark);background: var(--shiki-github-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-github-dark-text-decoration);}html.github-dark .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-github-dark);background: var(--shiki-github-dark-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-github-dark-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-github-dark-text-decoration);}html pre.shiki code .ssxIu, html code.shiki .ssxIu{--shiki-default:#24292E;--shiki-github-dark:#E1E4E8}html pre.shiki code .svdQ7, html code.shiki .svdQ7{--shiki-default:#D73A49;--shiki-github-dark:#F97583}html pre.shiki code .sJ6F3, html code.shiki .sJ6F3{--shiki-default:#032F62;--shiki-github-dark:#9ECBFF}html pre.shiki code .sIsaT, html code.shiki .sIsaT{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-github-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .snvgF, html code.shiki .snvgF{--shiki-default:#005CC5;--shiki-github-dark:#79B8FF}html pre.shiki code .sdCPZ, html code.shiki .sdCPZ{--shiki-default:#6A737D;--shiki-github-dark:#6A737D}html pre.shiki code .sk71V, html code.shiki .sk71V{--shiki-default:#22863A;--shiki-github-dark:#85E89D}",{"title":31,"